# The VM runs a release needs (release.md section 8, I76). tests/win/vm-run.sh check COMMIT reads
# this file as committed in COMMIT and passes only when every row has one passing record
# (tests/win/vm-run.sh run SNAPSHOT SUITE --record) for COMMIT and its TEST payload.json, made with
# COMMIT's scripts, and no failed one. One row a line:
#   SUITE  ARCH  SNAPSHOT     ARCH: the VM's own (arm64, x64); SNAPSHOT: its name (the rest of the
#                             line) or its {id}
# smoke is vm-run.sh's own check, never a release's. arm64 only: rb-win-template is an ARM64 VM;
# whether x64 under Prism there fills an x64 row, or x64 is the real PC's round only, is the
# owner's question. The cases no suite drives are in by-hand.md (never a pass here).
# worker: the shipped worker and bridge (release.md section 8: install through the shipped
# worker, rekordbox with the shipped bridge, a cache hit on each newly listed version), by
# worker.suite. Its cache-hit step SKIPs until a step can load a track in rekordbox, so its record
# isn't a pass and check fails on this row: no release with an uncarried Windows worker or bridge
# passes (whether a recorded by-hand W13a round may stand in is the owner's open question).
bootstrap  arm64  clean Windows
uninstall  arm64  clean Windows
update     arm64  clean Windows
platform   arm64  clean Windows
worker     arm64  rekordbox 7.2.19 logged in
